# Two builds of the kissfft program give identical objects, archives and image.
# %{msil_det} builds the program of ../kissfft/kissfft.test twice at -O2, in two
# directories from relative paths, and compares every CIL object (bitcode under
# lto), the archives that llvm-ar writes and msil-ld's image byte for byte
# (plan 5.12.4, 5.12.9; M23). check-recipe.py fails when the REDEFINE lines
# here differ from that test's, so both build the same program.
# REQUIRES: msil-corpus-kissfft
# REDEFINE: %{msil_srcs} = %S/../kissfft/kissfft_main.c
# REDEFINE: %{msil_archives} = kiss=%{msil_corpus}/kissfft-2a1f1337160e/kiss_fft.c, \
# REDEFINE:   %{msil_corpus}/kissfft-2a1f1337160e/kiss_fftr.c;sup=%S/../support/sup_arena.c, \
# REDEFINE:   %S/../support/sup_malloc.c,%S/../support/sup_memcmp.c,%S/../support/sup_memset.c, \
# REDEFINE:   %S/../support/sup_memcpy.c,%S/../support/sup_strlen.c,%S/../support/sup_out.c
# REDEFINE: %{msil_copts} = -isystem %S/../shim -I%S/../support \
# REDEFINE:   -I%{msil_corpus}/kissfft-2a1f1337160e -DNDEBUG -Dkiss_fft_scalar=double \
# REDEFINE:   -ffp-contract=off -Werror=implicit-function-declaration -w
# RUN: %python %S/check-recipe.py %s %S/../kissfft/kissfft.test
# RUN: %{msil_det}
